data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","content_index":0,"item_id":"msg_0d2e06ddb0540542006a70fa61e53881948c230bfff6edfeb6","logprobs":[],"output_index":2,"sequence_number":133,"text":"Today is **Monday, August 3, 2026**. Here are the most recent, credible “Azure AI”–related items I can find **as of today** (including Azure AI Foundry / Microsoft Foundry, which is where a lot of Azure’s AI platform news lands now):\n\n## Today (Aug 3, 2026)\n- **Azure service update (not strictly “Azure AI,” but Azure platform news today):** Azure posted a GA update about **immutability for the most recent seven days of backups on Azure SQL Database and Azure SQL Managed Instance**. ([azurecharts.com](https://azurecharts.com/updates?monthback=0))  \n  *Why it matters to Azure AI users:* many AI apps rely on Azure SQL-backed operational data; backup immutability is a security/resilience enhancement relevant to AI workloads too.\n\n- **Customer/partner news touching Microsoft Cloud + AI:** ArcelorMittal announced an expanded collaboration with **Microsoft Cloud and AI**. ([manilatimes.net](https://www.manilatimes.net/2026/08/03/tmt-newswire/globenewswire/arcelormittal-reshaping-digital-backbone-with-microsoft-cloud-and-ai/2396730))  \n  *Note:* this is broader “Microsoft Cloud and AI” rather than a specific Azure AI feature release.\n\n## Very recent (last week-ish)\n- **Model/platform availability via Foundry ecosystem:** Coverage indicates Moonshot AI’s **Kimi K3** reaching enterprise users via **Fireworks on Microsoft Foundry**, giving Azure customers a managed route to run the model. ([technode.com](https://technode.com/2026/07/30/moonshot-ais-kimi-k3-reaches-enterprise-users-through-fireworks-on-microsoft-foundry/))  \n- **Enterprise AI security direction:** Reporting on **Microsoft + Nvidia** pushing “active defense” style enterprise AI security (relevant to how Azure AI deployments are secured/operated). ([redmondmag.com](https://redmondmag.com/articles/2026/07/29/microsoft-